  "aiContextParagraph": "Constitution Day, marking the adoption of the Indian Constitution, saw widespread political discourse across the country as various parties held commemorations and protests. The Bharatiya Janata Party and the Congress party exchanged public critiques, with BJP leaders accusing Congress of historical misuse of constitutional provisions and policies. Conversely, Congress officials maintained that the ruling party poses a threat to democratic integrity. Beyond federal party disputes, several localized events occurred, including a torchlight procession in Delhi led by Minister of State Savitri Thakur, who advocated for the eradication of child marriage by 2030. Other activities included public rallies and institutional observations, such as those held at the South Coast Railway headquarters and academic institutions. These events underscored ongoing debates regarding the interpretation and application of constitutional principles in contemporary Indian governance.",
